      "section_number": "5.2.1",
      "section_heading": "Fundamental Types",
      "html_anchor": "fundamental-types",
      "html_line_start": 3019,
      "html_line_end": 3063,
      "pdf_page": 54,
      "exact_quote": "A fundamental type specifies both a basic type and a size. Register variables are always of a fundamental type, and instructions operate on these types. The same type-size specifiers are used for both variable definitions and for typing instructions, so their names are intentionally short.\nMost instructions have one or more type specifiers, needed to fully specify instruction behavior. Operand types and sizes are checked against instruction types for compatibility.",
